PUBLIC RESPONSE: C. Kd4

The promotion is poisoned. 1.a8=Q is met by 1...Nxa8 and the queen is lost with no compensation, the a8 queen does not even give check because the c6 pawn blocks the a8-e4 diagonal.  

The king is the active piece.  After 1.Kd4 the white king gets one step closer to f5 while the d3 knight stays on e5 and f4.

* e4 and e5 are covered by the king on d4 and the knight still covers e5 and f4;
* g4 is still blocked by its own pawn and e6 by its own pawn;
* f4 is covered by Nd3;
* the only real flight squares left to f5 are g5, f6 and g6.

Moving the knight away with Nc5 or Nf4 loses the current e5/f4 control of Nd3 and opens e5 to the black king, and Kf2 moves the white king away from the action.  b4 does nothing to improve the mating net.  Kd4 is the waiting/zugzwang improvement that keeps the Nd3 cover intact and brings the white king into mating distance.

